NNAAMMEE
       lsns - list namespaces

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       llssnnss [options] _n_a_m_e_s_p_a_c_e

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       llssnnss lists information about all the currently accessible namespaces or
       about the given _n_a_m_e_s_p_a_c_e. The _n_a_m_e_s_p_a_c_e identifier is an inode number.

       The default output is subject to change. So whenever possible, you
       should avoid using default outputs in your scripts. Always explicitly
       define expected output mode (----ttrreeee or ----lliisstt) and columns by using the
       ----oouuttppuutt option together with a columns list in environments where a
       stable output is required.

       The NNSSFFSS column, printed when nneett is specified for the ----ttyyppee option,
       is special; it uses multi-line cells. Use the option ----nnoowwrraapp to switch
       to ","-separated single-line representation.

       Note that llssnnss reads information directly from the _/_p_r_o_c filesystem and
       for non-root users it may return incomplete information. The current
       _/_p_r_o_c filesystem may be unshared and affected by a PID namespace (see
       uunnsshhaarree ----mmoouunntt--pprroocc for more details). llssnnss is not able to see
       persistent namespaces without processes where the namespace instance is
       held by a bind mount to /proc/_p_i_d/ns/_t_y_p_e.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --JJ, ----jjssoonn
           Use JSON output format.

       --ll, ----lliisstt
           Use list output format.

       --nn, ----nnoohheeaaddiinnggss
           Do not print a header line.

       --oo, ----oouuttppuutt _l_i_s_t
           Specify which output columns to print. Use ----hheellpp to get a list of
           all supported columns.

           The default list of columns may be extended if _l_i_s_t is specified in
           the format ++_l_i_s_t (e.g., llssnnss --oo ++PPAATTHH).

       ----oouuttppuutt--aallll
           Output all available columns.

       --pp, ----ttaasskk _P_I_D
           Display only the namespaces held by the process with this _P_I_D.

       --rr, ----rraaww
           Use the raw output format.

       --tt, ----ttyyppee _t_y_p_e
           Display the specified _t_y_p_e of namespaces only. The supported types
           are mmnntt, nneett, iippcc, uusseerr, ppiidd, uuttss, ccggrroouupp and ttiimmee. This option may
           be given more than once.

       --uu, ----nnoottrruunnccaattee
           Do not truncate text in columns.

       --WW, ----nnoowwrraapp
           Do not use multi-line text in columns.

       --TT, ----ttrreeee _r_e_l
           Use tree-like output format. If pprroocceessss is given as _r_e_l, print
           process tree(s) in each name space. This is default when ----ttrreeee is
           not specified. If ppaarreenntt is given, print tree(s) constructed by the
           parent/child relationship. If oowwnneerr is given, print tree(s)
           constructed by the owner/owned relationship. oowwnneerr is used as
           default when _r_e_l is omitted.

       --hh, ----hheellpp
           Display help text and exit.

       --VV, ----vveerrssiioonn
           Print version and exit.

